{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1126464-looking-for-help-on-bane-plot","id":1126464,"title":"looking for help on Bane plot","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-08T15:09:02-07:00","id":1126464,"title":"looking for help on Bane plot","content":"I am looking for advice on a plot I intend to run. The scenario is a series of events where humans are having their senses or consciousness expanded as a result of various experiments (which they don't know are being done to them). To summarize the results of how these humans have/will changed.<br /> <br /> 1) They experience synesthesia (the stimulation of one sense activates another sense, people who have it can &quot;smell colors&quot;, &quot;taste sounds,&quot; and the like.<br /> <br /> 2) They get bonuses to the Enigmas ability.<br /> <br /> 3) They are now immune to the Delerium. They can see Crinos form as what it is as well as various Fomori and monsters that would also normally be hidden because of it.<br /> <br /> 4) They are now considered to be in contact with the Periphery and therefore contact with the spirit world.<br /> <br /> 5) Contact is not limited to the Gaian Penumbra, but also the High and Dark Umbra.<br /> <br /> 6) Eventually their senses will develop the equivalent of Gifts like Sight From Beyond, Sense the Unnatural, and Pulse of the Invisible.<br /> <br /> It turns out that these people are the victims of experiments conducted by a group of occultists/paranormal enthusiasts who are testing their theories before they do it to themselves. It'll turn out that what is truly behind this group is a powerful Bane (like an Incarna with various lesser powered servitors). The concept of the Bane is that it weakens the Gauntlet so that it is easier for Malfean spirits to come back and forth (or perhaps even the Pattern Web holding the Tellurian together). The group itself aren't actually Wyrm cultists. They just don't know what they are dealing with. What this group is doing won't lead to any catastrophe so the plot is very self contained, and indeed is potentially solvable with minimal use of violence.<br /> <br /> What I am looking for are canonical elements that I can associate with this such as specific (named) totems, spirits, and other Wyrm lore. Any other comments are also welcomed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T15:31:40-07:00","id":1126474,"title":"","content":"The fact that some of the alterations start out like drug trips suggests that The Dark Fungus totem could be an instigator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T15:41:08-07:00","id":1126480,"title":"","content":"Are you saying the Bane itself is able to weaken the Gauntlet so that the experiments can work, or that the experiments themselves are going to weaken the Gauntlet in some way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T15:49:20-07:00","id":1126482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1126464-looking-for-help-on-bane-plot?p=1126480#post1126480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you saying the Bane itself is able to weaken the Gauntlet so that the experiments can work, or that the experiments themselves are going to weaken the Gauntlet in some way?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thread the hyphae through the Gauntlet, and it will be consumed and replaced...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T16:21:39-07:00","id":1126498,"title":"","content":"Sorry, my question was for the original poster, but you beat me to the &quot;Post Reply&quot; button. If the Bane is the one weakening the Gauntlet, your suggestion makes sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.